@ 36.2 - Sin Sukchu to Guānhuà
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Coblin, W. South (2000), “A Diachronic Study of Míng Guānhuà
# 			Phonology”. Monumenta Serica 48:267 – 335
	# Initials:
	b d dz ɡ > {p,pʼ} {t,tʼ} {ts,tsʼ} {k,kʼ}
	ŋ > ∅ / _{i,j,w,y}
	ŋ > ∅ / _u / _V
	w > u / _V
	v ʋ > f v
	z > {s,tsʼ} (the former “without exception” “in oblique tone words”)
	
	ɖʐ > ʈʂʼ / “in píng-tone syllables”
	ʐ > ʂ
	r > ʐ (Apparently there was some situation where this went to ∅, and then something
				happened with the output syllable being [ɚ])
	ʔ > ŋ / _V:[-high]
	ʔ > ∅ / _{j,i,y}
	ʔ > ∅ / _u (not always? Perhaps some variation with [ɣ] here?)
	ɣ > x
	j > i
	There seems to ahve been some stuff going on with palatalized [ŋ] > {ɲ,n} but it seems highly dialectal and I’m not entirely sure just what exactly
				was going on here
	w > {v,u}
	uj > (ɣ)u
	# Finals:
	m > n
	long-tail vowel thing > i (or [truncated vowel-thing] “where GH sibilant initial variants occur”)
	{long-tail vowel thingʔ,əʔ} > ɛʔ
	i > [long-tail vowel thing] / C̣_
	iʔ iw > eʔ ew / C̣_
	iʔ > ieʔ (> i[truncated vowel-thing]ʔ?)
	uʔ > oʔ
	uj > u(ɛ)i / m_
	uj > uɛi / {P,C:[+guttural],∅}_
	uj > ui / {C:[+dental],C:[+sibilant]}_
	ujʔ > uɛʔ
	un > uɛn / ! {C:[+dental],C:[+sibilant]}_
	uɛn > ɛn / ʋ_
	uŋ > oŋ (in one source?)
	juŋ > iuŋ / _{∅,x,ʋ,ʔ}
	juŋ > iuŋ / _ɡ:[+píng tone]
	juŋ > uŋ
	jujŋ ujŋ > iuŋ uŋ
	y > ɥ (> y~u dialectally?) / C̣_
	yʔ > yɛʔ / {l,C:[+dental +sibilant]}_ in “QYS -juət-type” finals, dialectally?
	yʔ > oʔ
	yʔ > yʔ(~yɛʔ?) / {∅,C:[+guttural]}, in -juət-types
	yʔ > ioʔ (> iʊʔ dialectally?) / {∅,C:[+guttural]}_, in -k-types
	yʔ > {ɥʔ,yʔ,uʔ} / C̣, in -juət-types
	yʔ > oʔ (> ʊʔ?) / C̣_, in -k-types
	yjʔ > yʔ
	yn > un / C̣_
	je jeʔ yeʔ > ɛ ɛʔ uɛʔ / C̣_
	je jeʔ > iɛ iɛʔ
	yeʔ > yɛʔ
	ye jej > yɛ i
	jew > au / C̣(C?)_
	jew > iau / _ // C̣(C?)_
	{jem,jen} > iɛn
	yen > uɛn / C̣_
	yen > yɛn
	ɔ > a
	wɔ > ɔ
	wɔʔ > uɔʔ / C:[+guttural]_
	wɔʔ > ɔʔ / _ // C:[+guttural]_
	ɔn > an; “[t]his final occurs exclusively after SR gutturals”
	wɔn ja wa > uɔn ia ua
	aʔ > ɔʔ / C:[+guttural]_
	jaʔ > iaʔ
	waʔ > aʔ / C:[+labiodental]_
	waʔ > uaʔ
	aj jaj waj aw jaw > ai iai uai au iau
	awʔ > ɔʔ
	{jawʔ,wawʔ} > ɔʔ / C̣_
	jawʔ wawʔ > iɔʔ uɔʔ
	am > an
	{jam,jan} > iɛn
	wan > an / C:[+labiodental]_
	wan > uan / _ // C:[+labiodental]_
	aŋ jaŋ > uaŋ aŋ / C̣_
	waŋ > uaŋ
	əjʔ əw {əm,ən} > eʔ ɛu ɛn
	əjŋ > ɛn (varies with ɛn?)
	# Tones:
	# qı̄ng píng > yı̄n píng
	# zhuó píng > yáng píng
	# qı̄ng shăng > shăng
	# zhuó shăng > qù
	# (There seems to be some conflict between shăng tones and qù tones, the latter noted
	# 			as being the spoken forms)